# SpotSet — build-time configuration. Copy to `.env.local` and fill in.
#
# 🔴 ONLY the anon / publishable key belongs here. It is safe in the bundle ONLY
#    because `force row level security` is on every table (migrations 0001/0002)
#    — the key identifies the project, it does not authorise anything.
#    The service_role key must NEVER appear in this repo, in a .env file, or in
#    any committed artifact: pih-dev/PTApp is PUBLIC, and that key bypasses RLS
#    by design. It lives in C:/projects/_archive/PTApp/supabase-spotset.env,
#    outside the working tree, where the sanity scripts read it from.
#
# With these unset the app builds and behaves exactly as it does today: src/auth.js
# reports `isAuthConfigured() === false` and every identity path stays dark.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<the publishable / anon key>
